{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794347940453,"sessionID":"ses_e388ef7b3ffe6Zgw16QrQo7dsU","part":{"id":"prt_1c778ba50001I7nuZz3wqoL5ld","messageID":"msg_1c778a0430010aS160CaKn24we","sessionID":"ses_e388ef7b3ffe6Zgw16QrQo7dsU","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347940453,"sessionID":"ses_e388ef7b3ffe6Zgw16QrQo7dsU","part":{"id":"prt_1c778ba520010tHB3XfvwCJpPp","messageID":"msg_1c778a0430010aS160CaKn24we","sessionID":"ses_e388ef7b3ffe6Zgw16QrQo7dsU","type":"text","text":"The 405 is because `POST /api/nope` doesn't match the GET catch-all; that's fine behavior. But better to handle 405 on API paths too. Let me fix CSRF order (it already is before recipient — wait, line 344 is before 348). Let me re-check: the bad csrf test used `'csrf_token':'nope'` in body but also had `X-CSRF-Token` valid in header `h2`, so `csrf_ok` returned True via header. That's correct precedence — header wins. The 404 was recipient not found. So actually not a bug. Let me verify with a bad header instead.","time":{"start":1794347940434,"end":1794347940450}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794347940879,"sessionID":"ses_e388ef7b3ffe6Zgw16QrQo7dsU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bb1a4ca574e9324b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"BANK_DATA_DIR=/workspace/data .venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,'backend')\nimport app as a\nc=a.app.test_client()\nr=c.post('/api/auth/login',json={'username':'alice','password':'pw'}); h={'Authorization':'Bearer '+r.json['token']}\nprint('bad csrf header only',c.post('/api/transfers',json={'to_username':'x','amount':1},headers={**h,'X-CSRF-Token':'nope'}).status_code)\nprint('bad csrf body only',c.post('/api/transfers',json={'to_username':'x','amount':1,'csrf_token':'nope'},headers=h).status_code)\nprint('no csrf',c.post('/api/transfers',json={'to_username':'x','amount':1},headers=h).status_code)\n\"","timeout":120000,"workdir":"/workspace"},"output":"bad csrf header only 403\nbad csrf body only 403\nno csrf 404\n","metadata":{"output":"bad csrf header only 403\nbad csrf body only 403\nno csrf 404\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"BANK_DATA_DIR=/workspace/data .venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,'backend')\nimport app as a\nc=a.app.test_client()\nr=c.post('/api/auth/login',json={'username':'alice','password':'pw'}); h={'Authorization':'Bearer '+r.json['token']}\nprint('bad csrf header only',c.post('/api/transfers',json={'to_username':'x','amount':1},headers={**h,'X-CSRF-Token':'nope'}).status_code)\nprint('bad csrf body only',c.post('/api/transfers',json={'to_username':'x','amount':1,'csrf_token':'nope'},headers=h).status_code)\nprint('no csrf',c.post('/api/transfers',json={'to_username':'x','amount':1},headers=h).status_code)\n\"","time":{"start":1794347940441,"end":1794347940824}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c778ba55001owvXsZi4X5fIRc","sessionID":"ses_e388ef7b3ffe6Zgw16QrQo7dsU","messageID":"msg_1c778a0430010aS160CaKn24we"}}
